WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.410 --> 00:00:03.923
<v Examiner>Detecting and treating genetic disease.

2
00:00:03.923 --> 00:00:04.631
<v Examiner>Four marks.

3
00:00:05.081 --> 00:00:08.946
<v Examiner>Explain some of the ways genetic abnormalities are detected,

4
00:00:08.946 --> 00:00:11.781
<v Examiner>including genetic testing and fetal testing,

5
00:00:11.781 --> 00:00:15.001
<v Examiner>and what genetic engineering and gene therapy are.

6
00:00:15.451 --> 00:00:18.104
The hook: look, sample, change, treat.

7
00:00:18.104 --> 00:00:19.220
Look at the DNA.

8
00:00:19.220 --> 00:00:20.337
Sample the baby.

9
00:00:20.337 --> 00:00:21.384
Change the DNA.

10
00:00:21.384 --> 00:00:22.641
Treat the patient.

11
00:00:23.091 --> 00:00:23.447
Look.

12
00:00:23.447 --> 00:00:28.008
Genetic testing reads a person's DNA, often from a blood sample,

13
00:00:28.008 --> 00:00:30.930
for genes or variants that cause disease.

14
00:00:30.930 --> 00:00:34.992
For example, a karyotype, which looks at the chromosomes.

15
00:00:34.992 --> 00:00:38.199
Or a molecular karyotype, called a CGH array,

16
00:00:38.199 --> 00:00:42.547
which checks thousands of positions for missing or extra DNA.

17
00:00:42.997 --> 00:00:44.106
Sample the baby.

18
00:00:44.106 --> 00:00:45.909
There are two fetal tests.

19
00:00:45.909 --> 00:00:50.693
Chorionic villus sampling, or CVS: tissue is taken from the placenta,

20
00:00:50.693 --> 00:00:52.426
at eight to twelve weeks.

21
00:00:52.426 --> 00:00:57.418
And amniocentesis: amniotic fluid is taken, at fourteen to twenty weeks.

22
00:00:57.418 --> 00:01:02.687
In both, the fetal cells are examined for chromosomal and genetic disorders.

23
00:01:04.137 --> 00:01:04.644
Change.

24
00:01:04.644 --> 00:01:08.702
Genetic engineering is the deliberate alteration of DNA,

25
00:01:08.702 --> 00:01:11.599
to change an organism's genetic make-up.

26
00:01:11.599 --> 00:01:14.932
Her example: bacteria altered to make insulin.

27
00:01:15.382 --> 00:01:15.770
Treat.

28
00:01:15.770 --> 00:01:21.522
Gene therapy is the treatment of a genetic disease by inserting genetic material into the

29
00:01:21.522 --> 00:01:24.107
patient's cells, carried in by a vector.

30
00:01:25.557 --> 00:01:26.222
The traps.

31
00:01:26.222 --> 00:01:30.009
CVS is earlier, eight to twelve weeks, from the placenta.

32
00:01:30.009 --> 00:01:34.327
Amniocentesis is later, fourteen to twenty weeks, from the fluid.

33
00:01:34.327 --> 00:01:38.048
Second: genetic engineering changes DNA in any organism,

34
00:01:38.048 --> 00:01:40.440
while gene therapy treats a patient.

35
00:01:40.440 --> 00:01:44.758
Third: a karyotype shows the number and shape of the chromosomes.

36
00:01:44.758 --> 00:01:48.213
It can't see a single-gene change like Huntington's.

37
00:01:48.663 --> 00:01:49.264
<v Examiner>Once more.

38
00:01:49.264 --> 00:01:51.607
<v Examiner>Detecting and treating genetic disease.

39
00:01:54.057 --> 00:01:59.300
Genetic testing reads a person's DNA, often from a blood sample: a karyotype,

40
00:01:59.300 --> 00:02:02.024
or a CGH array for missing or extra DNA.

41
00:02:02.024 --> 00:02:06.518
Chorionic villus sampling takes placenta at eight to twelve weeks.

42
00:02:06.518 --> 00:02:10.807
Amniocentesis takes amniotic fluid at fourteen to twenty weeks.

43
00:02:10.807 --> 00:02:12.646
Both check the fetal cells.

44
00:02:12.646 --> 00:02:16.459
Genetic engineering is the deliberate alteration of DNA,

45
00:02:16.459 --> 00:02:19.046
like bacteria altered to make insulin.

46
00:02:19.046 --> 00:02:24.902
Gene therapy treats a genetic disease by inserting genetic material into the patient's

47
00:02:24.902 --> 00:02:25.311
cells.
